  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Development Strengthened
At least 2 PFM Reform initiatives launched
Enhancing Effectiveness of MOF Assistance Programs
Professional assistance provided to ministerial support teams</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Strategic planning forums have not been institutionalized. No established M&amp;E system to monitor, track and report on the execution of short and long-term goals and no competency framework available 
- No Internal Audit function exists in other entities and there is no established measure to get accurate and up-to-date financial information to better manage financial risks of state owned economic authorities and enterprises
- There are significant financial distortions on the regulatory and commercial levels. No economic impact assessment of distortion and analysis on investment opportunities available.
- Operational capacity of Macro-Fiscal Policy Unit needs to be improved.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Organizing a strategic planning forum to institutionalize strategic management.
- Creating a pilot structure to support and manage the approved M&amp;E
- Engaging pilot internal audit and introducing internal audit to line ministries
- Suggesting mechanisms for gap closures in Egypt&#x2019;s subsidy system in assigned sectors.
- Preparing the budget for the next fiscal year and analyzing the actual performance of the current year
- Capacity development to executive support team.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 2 strategy documents for period 2020-2023 have been approved and finalized
- Organized 2 workshops on strategic thinking for senior/middle management, participated by 83 participants as well as cascading trainings for 136 government staff
- Developed the first MOF end of year M&amp;E strategy report
- Conducted Training Boot Camp for around 100 staff of the next generation
- Developed competency framework for the national debt management unit in MoF
- Conducted 3 full-scale internal audit for 3 departments in MoF and 1 authority related with MoF
- Reviewed various guarantees for Egyptian National Railways and National Authority for Tunnels and started to prepare for training programme on assessing risks of guarantee in partnership with the World Bank 
- Participated in the preparation of the draft budget for FY 2020/2021, jointly with the budget department and monitored 2019/20 budget execution through monthly analytical tables
- Created shock scenarios taking into account the impacts of COVID-19 on the economy and the state budget</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen institutional development within Ministry of Finance, MOF by launching of at least 2 Public Finance Management Reform initiatives, enhancing the effectiveness of MOF Assistance Programs, and providing professional assistance to ministerial support teams</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Annual M&amp;E report finalized and delivered 
- Launching of soft skills e-learning content development project for Taxes where 18 e-Content Modules were developed and approved.
- Audit Unit has been established and embedded in the new organizational structure 
- Designed Fiscal Commitments and Constringent Liabilities Framework 
- Egypt Project Preparation Facility has been approved 
- 5 one-stop-shop centers have been established in 5 governorates as pilots for all MOF services</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Strengthen institutional development within Ministry of Finance, MOF by launching of at least 2 Public Finance Management Reform initiatives, enhancing the effectiveness of MOF Assistance Programs, and providing professional assistance to ministerial support teams</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Conducted yearly in- house training for newly promoted General Managers. 
- Conducted 7 strategic planning forums; cascading forums and Strategy Alignment forums for around 400 MOF Middle and Top Management 
- Two rounds of workshops have been done to 2nd grade Governmental staff for around 80 candidates
- Launching of soft skills e-learning content development project for the Taxes Authority
- Conducted 4 full scale Audits and 1 Follow up audit on 5 of MOFs central departments and specialized units and 3 for MOFs affiliates
- Finalized preparation of the budget for FY 2021/2022, jointly with the budget department. 
- Updated pensions&#x2019; model and developed scenario analysis for the social insurance funds performance in addition to drafting reform strategy for pensions system for the coming ten years.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
